		<!--
			Tells iOS the app expects remote (push) notifications and may
			be woken in the background to handle them. Strictly speaking
			visible notifications (with a 'notification' payload) display
			even without this, but adding it future-proofs us against any
			data-only / content-available pushes the backend might send,
			and it's what Firebase's iOS setup guide recommends.
		-->
		<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
